  "question": {
    "text": "The coefficient of thermal expansion of a rod is temperature-dependent and is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3.465</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> in <math><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. If the length of the rod is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> at temperature <math><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, then the temperature at which the length will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></math> is [Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn></math>]",
